IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mhw-dates`
IMPORT `mhw-rules`

-- Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) -- the questions of the PERSON THE ACT IS APPLIED TO: the person examined
-- for, or made subject to, an assessment order, a court assessment order, a temporary treatment order or a treatment
-- order; a patient asked to consent to treatment, electroconvulsive treatment or neurosurgery; a person in a designated
-- mental health service who may be secluded or restrained; a party before the Mental Health Tribunal; and a consumer
-- with a complaint. The Act's terms with plain glosses; the practitioners', the authorised psychiatrist's, the chief
-- psychiatrist's, the Tribunal's and VCAT's judgments are inputs. Each question takes only plain facts (yes/no, numbers,
-- dates, a choice from a list); the duties with deadlines are DEONTIC rules run inside, from mhw-rules.l4.
--
-- Where a section is used by one question only, its words are applied here, with the quotation; the shared definitions
-- (ss 3, 4, 87), the criteria (ss 142, 143), the Tribunal's outcomes and the regulative rules are in mhw-rules.l4.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Mental Health
-- and Wellbeing Act 2022, Version No. 010 (30 September 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria;
-- published with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in
-- accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 -- the questions of the person the Act is applied to`

-- Who may act for the person, in ss 67(2), 206(2) and 226(2).
DECLARE `Who is acting` IS ONE OF
    `me`
    `a person I asked to act for me`
    `my guardian`
    `my parent`
    `a mental health advocate`
    `the DFFH Secretary, who has parental responsibility for me`
    `someone else`

§§ `Mental illness`

-- s 4, from mhw-rules.l4.
@export Would I be considered to have "mental illness" under the Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 4? Mental illness is a medical condition characterised by a significant disturbance of thought, mood, perception or memory; it cannot rest only on a person's opinions, beliefs, sexuality, conduct, drug or alcohol use, disability, status, distress or past diagnosis (s 4(2)).
GIVEN `do I have a medical condition significantly disturbing my thought, mood, perception or memory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a medical condition characterised by a significant disturbance of your thought, mood, perception or memory (a clinical judgment; answer as a clinician has assessed it)
      `is that only because of an s 4(2) matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only reason given is one or more of these: your political, religious or philosophical opinions or activity, sexual preference, gender identity or orientation, sexual behaviour, conduct against community standards, illegal or antisocial conduct, intellectual disability, drug or alcohol use, economic, social, cultural or racial status, family conflict, psychological distress, or a past diagnosis or treatment
      `is the reason the serious effects of drugs or alcohol` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the reason relied on is the serious temporary or permanent physical, biochemical or psychological effects of using drugs or alcohol (not the use itself), which may be an indication of mental illness (s 4(3))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Would I be considered to have mental illness` MEANS
    `s 4 -- mental illness` `do I have a medical condition significantly disturbing my thought, mood, perception or memory` `is that only because of an s 4(2) matter` `is the reason the serious effects of drugs or alcohol`

§§ `Assessment orders` -- arises if a doctor or authorised mental health practitioner has examined you, or an assessment order has been made

DECLARE `Assessment order answer` IS ONE OF
    `no assessment order may be made`
    `a community assessment order may be made, but not an inpatient one`
    `a community or an inpatient assessment order may be made`

-- s 144(1) "A registered medical practitioner or an authorised mental health practitioner may make an assessment order in
-- respect of a person if the practitioner -- (a) has examined the person within the previous 24 hours; and (b) is
-- satisfied that the compulsory assessment criteria apply to the person." s 145(2) "must not make an inpatient assessment
-- order ... unless the practitioner is satisfied that the person cannot be assessed in the community." An "if" and a
-- "must not ... unless": no order where they fail.
@export Can an assessment order be made on me (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 142, 144, 145), and can it be an inpatient order that lets me be taken to and kept at a mental health service? A doctor or authorised mental health practitioner who examined me within the previous 24 hours must be satisfied of all four compulsory assessment criteria.
GIVEN `how many hours ago was I examined` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours before the order was (or would be) made the practitioner examined you (s 144(1)(a) requires the previous 24 hours)
      `do I appear to have mental illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the practitioner is satisfied that you appear to have mental illness (s 142(a))
      `do I appear to need immediate treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the practitioner is satisfied that, because you appear to have mental illness, you appear to need immediate treatment to prevent serious deterioration in your mental or physical health, or serious harm to you or another person (s 142(b))
      `could I be assessed under the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the practitioner is satisfied that you can be assessed if made subject to the order (s 142(c))
      `are there no less restrictive means to assess me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the practitioner is satisfied that there are no less restrictive means reasonably available to assess you, for example voluntarily (s 142(d))
      `is the practitioner satisfied I cannot be assessed in the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the practitioner is satisfied that you cannot be assessed in the community (needed for an inpatient order, s 145(2))
GIVETH AN `Assessment order answer`
`Can an assessment order be made on me` MEANS
    IF     `how many hours ago was I examined` AT MOST 24
       AND `s 142 -- the compulsory assessment criteria apply` `do I appear to have mental illness` `do I appear to need immediate treatment` `could I be assessed under the order` `are there no less restrictive means to assess me`
    THEN IF `is the practitioner satisfied I cannot be assessed in the community`
         THEN `a community or an inpatient assessment order may be made`
         ELSE `a community assessment order may be made, but not an inpatient one`
    ELSE `no assessment order may be made`

DECLARE `Assessment order variation` IS ONE OF
    `not varied`
    `varied from inpatient to community`
    `varied from community to inpatient`

-- s 147 "(1) A community assessment order expires 24 hours after it is made. (2) An inpatient assessment order expires at
-- the earlier of the following -- (a) 24 hours after the assessment patient is received at a designated mental health
-- service; (b) 72 hours after the order is made." s 154 "(1) An inpatient assessment order that is varied to a community
-- assessment order expires at the earlier of the following -- (a) if the assessment patient had been received at a
-- designated mental health service before the variation of the order, 24 hours after the patient is received ...; (b)
-- 24 hours after the variation of the order. (2) A community assessment order that is varied to an inpatient assessment
-- order expires 24 hours after the variation of the order." s 165 "(1) ... may extend an assessment order for up to 24
-- hours ... (2) ... on no more than 2 occasions." An extension is read as adding its hours to the time of expiry (fork
-- F6); hours over 24, and a third extension, are not counted. s 227(3): custody does not change the time of expiry.
@export When does my assessment order expire (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 147, 154, 165)? The answer is the number of hours after the order was made. A community order lasts 24 hours; an inpatient order 24 hours after I arrive at the service, but no more than 72 hours after it was made; a variation restarts a 24-hour clock; the authorised psychiatrist may extend it twice, by up to 24 hours each time.
GIVEN `is it an inpatient assessment order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order was made as an inpatient assessment order (one that lets you be taken to and kept at a designated mental health service); answer for the order as first made
      `have I been received at the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been received (arrived) at a designated mental health service under the order
      `hours from the order to my arrival` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours after the order was made you were received at the service (0 if you have not been)
      `how was the order varied` IS AN `Assessment order variation` @desc Whether the order was varied: not varied, varied from inpatient to community, or varied from community to inpatient (ss 153, 154)
      `hours from the order to the variation` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours after the order was made it was varied (0 if it was not varied)
      `hours of the first extension` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours the authorised psychiatrist extended the order by the first time (0 if not extended); the Act allows up to 24
      `hours of the second extension` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours the authorised psychiatrist extended the order by the second time (0 if not extended twice); the Act allows up to 24
GIVETH A NUMBER
`When does my assessment order expire` MEANS
    `the expiry before any extension` PLUS (min `hours of the first extension` 24) PLUS (min `hours of the second extension` 24)
    WHERE
        `the unvaried expiry` MEANS
            IF `is it an inpatient assessment order`
            THEN IF `have I been received at the service`
                 THEN min (`hours from the order to my arrival` PLUS 24) 72
                 ELSE 72
            ELSE 24
        `the expiry before any extension` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how was the order varied`
            WHEN `not varied` THEN `the unvaried expiry`
            WHEN `varied from inpatient to community` THEN
                IF `have I been received at the service` AND `hours from the order to my arrival` AT MOST `hours from the order to the variation`
                THEN min (`hours from the order to my arrival` PLUS 24) (`hours from the order to the variation` PLUS 24)
                ELSE `hours from the order to the variation` PLUS 24
            WHEN `varied from community to inpatient` THEN `hours from the order to the variation` PLUS 24

-- s 165 "(1) An authorised psychiatrist ... may extend an assessment order for up to 24 hours if, after examining the
-- assessment patient, the authorised psychiatrist is not able to determine whether the compulsory treatment criteria
-- apply to that patient. (2) An assessment order may be extended under subsection (1) on no more than 2 occasions." An
-- "if" and a flat limit: JUST FALSE where either fails.
@export Can my assessment order be extended again (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 165)? The authorised psychiatrist may extend it by up to 24 hours, at most twice, only if after examining me they cannot yet decide whether the compulsory treatment criteria apply.
GIVEN `how many times has it been extended` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times the assessment order has already been extended (0, 1 or 2)
      `has the psychiatrist examined me and been unable to decide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist has examined you and is not able to determine whether the compulsory treatment criteria apply to you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my assessment order be extended again` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`how many times has it been extended` LESS THAN 2 AND `has the psychiatrist examined me and been unable to decide`)

-- s 160 "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an assessment patient must not be given treatment while the assessment order is
-- in force. (2) An assessment patient may be given treatment ... if -- (a) the patient gives informed consent to the
-- treatment; or (b) a registered medical practitioner employed or engaged by the responsible designated mental health
-- service is satisfied that urgent treatment must be given to the patient to prevent -- (i) serious deterioration in the
-- patient's mental or physical health; or (ii) serious harm to the patient or to another person." s 175 is the same for
-- a court assessment patient, adding "(c) the patient was subject to a temporary treatment order or treatment order
-- immediately before the court assessment order is made, and the temporary treatment order or treatment order is still
-- in force; or (d) an authorised psychiatrist makes a temporary treatment order in respect of the patient."
@export Can I be given treatment while I am on an assessment order or court assessment order (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 160, 175)? Without my informed consent, only urgent treatment a doctor of the service is satisfied must be given to prevent serious deterioration or serious harm (and, for a court assessment order, treatment under a treatment order).
GIVEN `is it a court assessment order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order is a court assessment order made by a court under the Sentencing Act 1991 (answer no for an ordinary assessment order)
      `do I give informed consent to the treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you give informed consent to the treatment (s 86)
      `is a doctor satisfied urgent treatment must be given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a registered medical practitioner employed or engaged by the mental health service is satisfied that urgent treatment must be given to you to prevent serious deterioration in your mental or physical health, or serious harm to you or another person
      `was I on a treatment order that is still in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a court assessment order: whether you were subject to a temporary treatment order or treatment order immediately before the court assessment order was made, and it is still in force
      `has a psychiatrist made a temporary treatment order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a court assessment order: whether an authorised psychiatrist has made a temporary treatment order for you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be treated while on an assessment order` MEANS
    `yes or no` (   `do I give informed consent to the treatment`
                 OR `is a doctor satisfied urgent treatment must be given`
                 OR (`is it a court assessment order` AND (`was I on a treatment order that is still in force` OR `has a psychiatrist made a temporary treatment order`)))

-- s 176 "An authorised psychiatrist must complete an assessment of a court assessment patient within 7 days -- (a) in the
-- case of a community court assessment order, after the order is made; or (b) in the case of an inpatient court
-- assessment order, after the person has been received at the designated mental health service ..." The last day is 7
-- days after that day (the day itself not counted, fork F1).
@export By when must the authorised psychiatrist complete my assessment under a court assessment order (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 176)? Within 7 days after the order is made (community) or after I am received at the mental health service (inpatient).
GIVEN `is it an inpatient court assessment order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court made an inpatient court assessment order (you are to be assessed at a designated mental health service) rather than a community one
      `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the court made the court assessment order
      `the day I was received at the service` IS A DATE @desc For an inpatient order, the day you were received at the designated mental health service (any date for a community order)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my court assessment be completed` MEANS
    IF `is it an inpatient court assessment order`
    THEN `the date` 7 `days after` `the day I was received at the service`
    ELSE `the date` 7 `days after` `the day the order was made`

§§ `Temporary treatment orders` -- arises if you are on an assessment order or court assessment order, or a temporary treatment order has been made

DECLARE `Temporary treatment order answer` IS ONE OF
    `no temporary treatment order may be made`
    `a community temporary treatment order may be made, but not an inpatient one`
    `a community or an inpatient temporary treatment order may be made`
    `s 180 does not reach me: I am not an assessment patient or court assessment patient`

-- s 180 "(1) An authorised psychiatrist may make a temporary treatment order in respect of an assessment patient or a
-- court assessment patient if the authorised psychiatrist -- (a) has examined the assessment patient or court
-- assessment patient; and (b) is satisfied that the compulsory treatment criteria apply ... (3) The person who makes a
-- temporary treatment order in respect of an assessment patient must not be the same person who made the assessment
-- order". s 181(2) "must not make an inpatient temporary treatment order ... unless ... satisfied that the patient cannot
-- be treated in the community." A person on no assessment order is outside s 180 (NOTHING-kind *limited by its own
-- wording*, given as its own answer). s 329 lets the power be delegated to a doctor of the service (not encoded).
@export Can a temporary treatment order be made on me (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 143, 180, 181), and can it be an inpatient order? An authorised psychiatrist who has examined me must be satisfied of all four compulsory treatment criteria, and must not be the person who made my assessment order.
GIVEN `what order am I on` IS AN `Order` @desc The order you are on now: no order, an assessment order, a court assessment order, a temporary treatment order, a treatment order, a secure or court secure treatment order, or a forensic patient order
      `has the psychiatrist examined me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist has examined you
      `do I have mental illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that you have mental illness (s 143(a))
      `do I need immediate treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that, because of the mental illness, you need immediate treatment to prevent serious deterioration in your mental or physical health, or serious harm to you or another person (s 143(b))
      `will the treatment be provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that the immediate treatment will be provided to you if you are made subject to the order (s 143(c))
      `are there no less restrictive means to treat me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that there are no less restrictive means reasonably available for you to receive the immediate treatment, for example voluntarily (s 143(d))
      `did the same person make my assessment order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the psychiatrist proposing the temporary treatment order is the same person who made your assessment order (answer no for a court assessment order)
      `is the psychiatrist satisfied I cannot be treated in the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that you cannot be treated in the community (needed for an inpatient order, s 181(2))
GIVETH A `Temporary treatment order answer`
`Can a temporary treatment order be made on me` MEANS
    IF NOT (`what order am I on` EQUALS `an assessment order` OR `what order am I on` EQUALS `a court assessment order`)
    THEN `s 180 does not reach me: I am not an assessment patient or court assessment patient`
    ELSE IF     `has the psychiatrist examined me`
            AND `s 143 -- the compulsory treatment criteria apply` `do I have mental illness` `do I need immediate treatment` `will the treatment be provided` `are there no less restrictive means to treat me`
            AND (NOT (`what order am I on` EQUALS `an assessment order` AND `did the same person make my assessment order`))
         THEN IF `is the psychiatrist satisfied I cannot be treated in the community`
              THEN `a community or an inpatient temporary treatment order may be made`
              ELSE `a community temporary treatment order may be made, but not an inpatient one`
         ELSE `no temporary treatment order may be made`

-- s 183 "A temporary treatment order expires 28 days after it is made, beginning on and including the day the order was
-- made." Day 1 is the day it was made, so its last day is the 28th day, 27 days later (fork F1). s 374(2): where the
-- Tribunal adjourns the hearing past that day for exceptional circumstances, it "may extend the duration of the
-- temporary treatment order ... for a period not exceeding 10 business days", once (s 374(3)); more than 10 is not
-- counted.
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE
      `business days extended` IS A NUMBER
      `weekday public holidays` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the temporary treatment order` `the day the order was made` `business days extended` `weekday public holidays` MEANS
    IF `business days extended` AT MOST 0
    THEN `the date` 27 `days after` `the day the order was made`
    ELSE `the last of` (min `business days extended` 10) `business days after` (`the date` 27 `days after` `the day the order was made`) `with` `weekday public holidays`

@export What is the last day of my temporary treatment order (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 183, 374)? It expires 28 days after it is made, counting the day it was made, unless the Tribunal extends it by up to 10 business days to adjourn the hearing.
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the authorised psychiatrist made the temporary treatment order
      `how many business days did the Tribunal extend it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many business days the Mental Health Tribunal extended the order when adjourning your hearing for exceptional circumstances (0 if none; the Act allows up to 10, once)
      `how many weekday public holidays fall in the extension` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the extension (0 if none or no extension); each moves the last day on one business day
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day of my temporary treatment order` MEANS
    `the last day of the temporary treatment order` `the day the order was made` `how many business days did the Tribunal extend it` `how many weekday public holidays fall in the extension`

-- s 189 "(1) Before a temporary treatment order expires, the Mental Health Tribunal must conduct a hearing to determine
-- whether to make a treatment order ... (2) Despite subsection (1), a hearing is not required if the temporary treatment
-- order is revoked before the hearing." The duty is run from mhw-rules.l4.
@export Did the Mental Health Tribunal hear my case before my temporary treatment order expired (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 189)? The Tribunal must hold a hearing on whether to make a treatment order before the temporary treatment order expires, unless the order is revoked first.
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the temporary treatment order was made
      `how many business days did the Tribunal extend it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many business days the Tribunal extended the order when adjourning the hearing (0 if none)
      `how many weekday public holidays fall in the extension` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the extension (0 if none)
      `was the order revoked before any hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the temporary treatment order was revoked before the Tribunal held a hearing
      `has the Tribunal held the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has conducted the hearing
      `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tribunal conducted the hearing (any date if it has not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Was my temporary treatment order heard in time` MEANS
    IF `was the order revoked before any hearing`
    THEN `not owed on these facts`
    ELSE `what became of the duty from` `the day the order was made` `to` (`the last day of the temporary treatment order` `the day the order was made` `how many business days did the Tribunal extend it` `how many weekday public holidays fall in the extension`) `under` `s 189(1) -- the Tribunal must hear me before my temporary treatment order expires` `owed by` `the Mental Health Tribunal` `to do` `hold the hearing` `done` `has the Tribunal held the hearing` `on` `the day of the hearing` `as at` `today`

§§ `Treatment orders and the Tribunal's decision` -- arises if you are on a temporary treatment order or treatment order

-- ss 192(2), 194(2), 207(2), (4), (5), from mhw-rules.l4.
@export What must the Mental Health Tribunal do at my hearing about a treatment order, or on my application to revoke my order (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 192, 194, 207)? If it is satisfied the compulsory treatment criteria apply it must make or confirm the order, and it may make it an inpatient order only if satisfied I cannot be treated in the community; if not satisfied, it must revoke the order.
GIVEN `is the Tribunal satisfied the criteria apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Mental Health Tribunal is satisfied that the compulsory treatment criteria apply to you (s 143: mental illness, need for immediate treatment to prevent serious deterioration or harm, the treatment will be provided, no less restrictive means)
      `is the Tribunal satisfied I cannot be treated in the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that you cannot be treated in the community
GIVETH A `Tribunal outcome`
`What must the Tribunal do at my hearing` MEANS
    `ss 192, 194, 207 -- what the Tribunal must do` `is the Tribunal satisfied the criteria apply` `is the Tribunal satisfied I cannot be treated in the community`

-- s 193 "The Mental Health Tribunal must specify the period of a treatment order, which must not exceed -- (a) if the
-- person is 18 years of age or over, 6 months; or (b) if the person is under 18 years of age, 3 months." Age is read at
-- the making of the order (fork F9).
@export What is the longest my treatment order can last, in months (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 193)? 6 months if I am 18 or over, 3 months if I am under 18.
GIVEN `my age when the order is made` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on the day the Tribunal makes the treatment order
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How long can my treatment order last` MEANS
    IF `my age when the order is made` AT LEAST 18 THEN 6 ELSE 3

@export What is the latest day my treatment order can run to (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 193)? The Tribunal sets the period, which must not exceed 6 months (3 months if I am under 18) from the day it is made.
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the Mental Health Tribunal made the treatment order
      `my age when the order is made` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years on that day
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the latest day my treatment order can run to` MEANS
    `the date` (`How long can my treatment order last` `my age when the order is made`) `months after` `the day the order was made`

DECLARE `Application timing` IS ONE OF
    `in time: at least 10 business days before the order expires`
    `late, but the principal registrar accepted it as reasonable in the circumstances`
    `late: the principal registrar may reject it`

-- s 191 "(1) An application under section 190 must -- (a) be made at least 10 business days before the expiry of the
-- current treatment order ... (2) Despite subsection (1)(a), the principal registrar may accept an application ... if --
-- (a) the application is made less than 10 business days before the expiry ...; and (b) the principal registrar is
-- satisfied that it is reasonable in the circumstances to accept the application." s 368(1)(b): the registrar "may
-- reject" an application lodged out of time. The business days are counted after the day of the application, up to and
-- including the last day of the order (fork F4).
@export Was the authorised psychiatrist's application for another treatment order made in time (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 191)? It must be made at least 10 business days before my current treatment order expires; a later one may be accepted only if the principal registrar is satisfied that is reasonable.
GIVEN `the day the application was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the authorised psychiatrist applied to the Mental Health Tribunal for another treatment order
      `the last day of my current order` IS A DATE @desc The last day your current treatment order is in force
      `how many weekday public holidays fall between them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday after the day of the application, up to the last day of your order
      `did the principal registrar accept a late application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal registrar was satisfied it was reasonable in the circumstances to accept the application although it was late
GIVETH AN `Application timing`
`Was the application for another treatment order in time` MEANS
    IF (`the weekdays after` `the day the application was made` `up to` `the last day of my current order`) MINUS `how many weekday public holidays fall between them` AT LEAST 10
    THEN `in time: at least 10 business days before the order expires`
    ELSE IF `did the principal registrar accept a late application`
         THEN `late, but the principal registrar accepted it as reasonable in the circumstances`
         ELSE `late: the principal registrar may reject it`

§§ `Changes to my order` -- arises if your temporary treatment order or treatment order is varied, or you are moved to another service

DECLARE `Order setting` IS ONE OF
    `a community order`
    `an inpatient order`

-- s 200 "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an authorised psychiatrist may vary -- (a) a community temporary treatment order to
-- an inpatient temporary treatment order; or (b) a community treatment order to an inpatient treatment order. (2) Before
-- varying ... an authorised psychiatrist -- (a) must be satisfied that the person who is subject to the order cannot be
-- treated in the community". A precondition: JUST FALSE where it fails; no answer for other orders (NOTHING-kind
-- *limited by its own wording*). s 200(3): the variation does not change how long the order lasts.
@export Can the authorised psychiatrist change my community temporary treatment order or community treatment order to an inpatient order (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 200)? Only if satisfied I cannot be treated in the community; it does not change how long the order lasts.
GIVEN `what order am I on` IS AN `Order` @desc The order you are on now (this question is about a temporary treatment order or a treatment order)
      `is it a community or an inpatient order` IS AN `Order setting` @desc Whether your order is now a community order or an inpatient order
      `is the psychiatrist satisfied I cannot be treated in the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that you cannot be treated in the community
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my order be changed to inpatient` MEANS
    IF     (`what order am I on` EQUALS `a temporary treatment order` OR `what order am I on` EQUALS `a treatment order`)
       AND `is it a community or an inpatient order` EQUALS `a community order`
    THEN `yes or no` `is the psychiatrist satisfied I cannot be treated in the community`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 204 "(1) Within 28 days after a community treatment order is varied to an inpatient treatment order, beginning on and
-- including the day the order was varied, the Mental Health Tribunal must conduct a hearing ... (2) Despite subsection
-- (1), a hearing is not required if the inpatient treatment order is revoked or varied to a community treatment order
-- before the hearing." The 28th day is 27 days after the day of the variation (fork F1). A temporary treatment order
-- varied to inpatient gets no s 204 hearing (finding 4).
@export Did the Mental Health Tribunal hear my case within 28 days after my community treatment order was changed to an inpatient treatment order (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 204)? The Tribunal must hold a hearing within 28 days, counting the day of the change, unless the order is revoked or changed back to a community order first.
GIVEN `was it a treatment order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order changed to inpatient was a treatment order made by the Tribunal (answer no for a temporary treatment order)
      `the day it was changed to inpatient` IS A DATE @desc The day the authorised psychiatrist varied your community treatment order to an inpatient treatment order
      `was it revoked or changed back before any hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the inpatient treatment order was revoked, or varied back to a community treatment order, before the Tribunal held a hearing
      `has the Tribunal held the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has conducted the hearing
      `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tribunal conducted the hearing (any date if it has not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Was my change to inpatient heard in time` MEANS
    IF (NOT `was it a treatment order`) OR `was it revoked or changed back before any hearing`
    THEN `not owed on these facts`
    ELSE `what became of the duty from` `the day it was changed to inpatient` `to` (`the date` 27 `days after` `the day it was changed to inpatient`) `under` `s 204(1) -- the Tribunal must hear me within 28 days after my order was made inpatient` `owed by` `the Mental Health Tribunal` `to do` `hold the hearing` `done` `has the Tribunal held the hearing` `on` `the day of the hearing` `as at` `today`

-- s 204(3), from mhw-rules.l4.
@export What must the Mental Health Tribunal do at the hearing about my treatment order being changed to inpatient (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 204(3))? Confirm the inpatient order if the criteria still apply and I cannot be treated in the community; change it back to a community order if I can be; revoke it if the criteria do not apply.
GIVEN `is the Tribunal satisfied the criteria still apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Mental Health Tribunal is satisfied that the compulsory treatment criteria still apply to you
      `is the Tribunal satisfied I cannot be treated in the community` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that you cannot be treated in the community (answer no if it is satisfied that you can be)
GIVETH A `Tribunal outcome`
`What must the Tribunal do about my change to inpatient` MEANS
    `s 204(3) -- what the Tribunal must do` `is the Tribunal satisfied the criteria still apply` `is the Tribunal satisfied I cannot be treated in the community`

-- s 226 "(1) Within 20 business days after an order is varied under section 223, the person who is subject to that order
-- may apply to the Mental Health Tribunal for a review ... (2) The following persons may apply ... on behalf of a person
-- ... within 20 business days after the order is varied -- (a) any person requested by the person subject to the order;
-- (b) any guardian ...; (c) a parent ..., if the person is under 16 years of age; (d) the DFFH Secretary, if that
-- Secretary has parental responsibility ...". A period the text fixes: late is JUST FALSE. A mental health advocate or
-- anyone else is not listed and the list is not closed: NOTHING (NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*; finding 5).
GIVEN `the day the order was varied` IS A DATE
      `weekday public holidays` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 226 -- the last day to apply for review of a transfer` `the day the order was varied` `weekday public holidays` MEANS
    `the last of` 20 `business days after` `the day the order was varied` `with` `weekday public holidays`

@export By when can I ask the Mental Health Tribunal to review the decision to move my assessment or treatment to another mental health service (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 226)? Within 20 business days after my order was varied.
GIVEN `the day my order was varied` IS A DATE @desc The day your court assessment order, temporary treatment order or treatment order was varied to name another designated mental health service (s 223)
      `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the period (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when can I ask for review of my transfer` MEANS
    `s 226 -- the last day to apply for review of a transfer` `the day my order was varied` `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days`

@export Can this person apply to the Mental Health Tribunal now for review of the decision to move my assessment or treatment to another mental health service (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 226)? I may apply, and so may a person I ask, my guardian, my parent if I am under 16, or the DFFH Secretary if they have parental responsibility for me, within 20 business days after the order was varied.
GIVEN `who is applying` IS A `Who is acting` @desc Who is applying: you, a person you asked to act for you, your guardian, your parent, a mental health advocate, the DFFH Secretary (who has parental responsibility for you under a child protection order), or someone else
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `the day my order was varied` IS A DATE @desc The day your order was varied to name another designated mental health service
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE @desc The day the application is (or would be) made to the Tribunal
      `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the period (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I ask for review of my transfer` MEANS
    IF `who is applying` EQUALS `a mental health advocate` OR `who is applying` EQUALS `someone else`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `yes or no` (    (NOT (`who is applying` EQUALS `my parent` AND `my age` AT LEAST 16))
                      AND (NOT (`the day of the application` `is after` (`s 226 -- the last day to apply for review of a transfer` `the day my order was varied` `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days`))))

§§ `Ending my order` -- arises if you are on an assessment order, temporary treatment order or treatment order

-- s 206 "(1) A person who is subject to a temporary treatment order or treatment order may apply at any time while the
-- order is in force to the Mental Health Tribunal for the order to be revoked. (2) The following persons may apply ... on
-- behalf of a person ... at any time while the order is in force ... (a) any person requested by the person subject to
-- the order; (b) any guardian ...; (c) a mental health advocate; (d) a parent ..., if the person is under 16 years of
-- age; (e) the DFFH Secretary, if that Secretary has parental responsibility ...". "while the order is in force" is a
-- period the text fixes: JUST FALSE outside it. Other orders, and anyone not listed: NOTHING (NOTHING-kind *limited by its
-- own wording*). The Tribunal must hear it "as soon as practicable" (s 207(1)).
@export Can this person apply to the Mental Health Tribunal to revoke my temporary treatment order or treatment order (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 206)? I may apply at any time while the order is in force, and so may a person I ask, my guardian, a mental health advocate, my parent if I am under 16, or the DFFH Secretary if they have parental responsibility for me.
GIVEN `what order am I on` IS AN `Order` @desc The order you are on (this question is about a temporary treatment order or a treatment order)
      `is the order in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order is still in force (it has not expired or been revoked)
      `who is applying` IS A `Who is acting` @desc Who is applying: you, a person you asked to act for you, your guardian, your parent, a mental health advocate, the DFFH Secretary (who has parental responsibility for you), or someone else
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply to revoke my order` MEANS
    IF     (NOT (`what order am I on` EQUALS `a temporary treatment order` OR `what order am I on` EQUALS `a treatment order`))
        OR `who is applying` EQUALS `someone else`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `yes or no` (`is the order in force` AND (NOT (`who is applying` EQUALS `my parent` AND `my age` AT LEAST 16)))

-- s 161 "An authorised psychiatrist must immediately revoke an assessment order if the authorised psychiatrist determines
-- that the compulsory treatment criteria do not apply to the assessment patient." s 205: the same for a temporary
-- treatment order or treatment order "if the authorised psychiatrist determines that the compulsory treatment criteria no
-- longer apply". A duty whose "if" is unmet: JUST FALSE, the duty is not engaged (fork F7). Other orders: NOTHING.
@export Must the authorised psychiatrist revoke my order now (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 161, 205)? Yes, immediately, once they determine that the compulsory treatment criteria do not (or no longer) apply to me.
GIVEN `what order am I on` IS AN `Order` @desc The order you are on (this question is about an assessment order, a temporary treatment order or a treatment order)
      `has the psychiatrist determined the criteria do not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist has determined that the compulsory treatment criteria do not apply, or no longer apply, to you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my psychiatrist revoke my order` MEANS
    IF    `what order am I on` EQUALS `an assessment order`
       OR `what order am I on` EQUALS `a temporary treatment order`
       OR `what order am I on` EQUALS `a treatment order`
    THEN `yes or no` `has the psychiatrist determined the criteria do not apply`
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Custody` IS ONE OF
    `not in custody`
    `in a prison`
    `in a youth justice custodial centre`
    `in a police gaol`
    `in immigration detention, not assessed or treated as an inpatient`
    `in immigration detention, but assessed or treated as an inpatient`

DECLARE `Order status` IS ONE OF
    `in force`
    `in force, but of no effect while I am detained in custody`
    `ended: it has expired`
    `ended: it has been revoked`

-- s 183 and s 193 (expiry); ss 205, 207(2)(b), 192(2)(b) (revocation); s 208 "A temporary treatment order is revoked if --
-- (a) a treatment order is made ...; or (b) a secure treatment order or court secure treatment order is made ...; or (c)
-- the temporary treatment patient is detained in a designated mental health service under section 30(2) or 30A(3) of the
-- Crimes (Mental Impairment and Unfitness to be Tried) Act 1997"; s 209 the same for a treatment order ("another
-- treatment order"); s 227 "(2) An order to which this section applies has no effect while a person who is subject to
-- the order is detained in custody. (3) An order ... expires at the time it would otherwise have expired ... (4) ... a
-- person is detained in custody if the person is held in -- (a) a prison ...; (b) a youth justice custodial centre; or
-- (c) a police gaol ...; or (d) immigration detention ..., unless the person is assessed or receives treatment as an
-- inpatient." Other orders: NOTHING.
@export Is my temporary treatment order or treatment order still in force today (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 183, 193, 205, 207, 208, 209, 227)? It ends when it expires or is revoked, including when a new treatment order or a secure treatment order is made; while I am held in prison, youth justice custody, a police gaol or immigration detention it has no effect, but it still expires on time.
GIVEN `what order am I on` IS AN `Order` @desc The order you are asking about (a temporary treatment order or a treatment order)
      `the last day of the order` IS A DATE @desc The last day the order is in force (28 days counting the day it was made for a temporary treatment order; the period the Tribunal set for a treatment order)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `has the psychiatrist or the Tribunal revoked it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist or the Mental Health Tribunal has revoked the order
      `has a new treatment order been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a treatment order (for a temporary treatment order) or another treatment order (for a treatment order) has been made for you
      `has a secure treatment order been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a secure treatment order or court secure treatment order has been made for you
      `am I detained under the Crimes (Mental Impairment) Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are detained in a designated mental health service under section 30(2) or 30A(3) of the Crimes (Mental Impairment and Unfitness to be Tried) Act 1997
      `am I in custody` IS A `Custody` @desc Whether you are held in custody today: not in custody, in a prison, a youth justice custodial centre, a police gaol, or immigration detention (and whether you are assessed or treated there as an inpatient)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Order status`
`Is my order still in force` MEANS
    IF NOT (`what order am I on` EQUALS `a temporary treatment order` OR `what order am I on` EQUALS `a treatment order`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `has the psychiatrist or the Tribunal revoked it` OR `has a new treatment order been made` OR `has a secure treatment order been made` OR `am I detained under the Crimes (Mental Impairment) Act`
         THEN JUST `ended: it has been revoked`
         ELSE IF `today` `is after` `the last day of the order`
              THEN JUST `ended: it has expired`
              ELSE IF `am I in custody` EQUALS `not in custody` OR `am I in custody` EQUALS `in immigration detention, but assessed or treated as an inpatient`
                   THEN JUST `in force`
                   ELSE JUST `in force, but of no effect while I am detained in custody`

§§ `Leave of absence` -- arises if you are kept at a designated mental health service as an inpatient

-- s 212 "(1) An authorised psychiatrist may grant a leave of absence ... to a person subject to one of the following
-- orders -- (a) an inpatient assessment order; (b) an inpatient court assessment order; (c) an inpatient temporary
-- treatment order; (d) an inpatient treatment order ... (3) If the person ... is subject to an inpatient treatment order
-- and an intensive monitored supervision order, an authorised psychiatrist may only grant a leave of absence ... (a) if
-- it is necessary for the person to receive urgent or necessary medical treatment at other premises; and (b) for a
-- maximum period of 7 days." For other orders the list is not closed by "only" (security patients have Part 10.4):
-- NOTHING. Under s 212(2) the purpose, period and conditions are what the psychiatrist is satisfied are appropriate.
@export Can I be granted leave of absence from the mental health service (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 212)? The authorised psychiatrist may grant leave, for a purpose and period they think appropriate, to a person on an inpatient assessment, court assessment, temporary treatment or treatment order; if I am also on an intensive monitored supervision order, only for urgent or necessary medical treatment elsewhere, and for at most 7 days.
GIVEN `what order am I on` IS AN `Order` @desc The order you are on
      `am I an inpatient under it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order is an inpatient order (you are kept at a designated mental health service)
      `am I also on an intensive monitored supervision order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are also subject to an intensive monitored supervision order (Chapter 12)
      `is the leave for urgent or necessary medical treatment elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the leave is needed for you to receive urgent or necessary medical treatment at other premises
      `how many days of leave` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of leave are sought
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be granted leave` MEANS
    IF NOT (`am I an inpatient under it` AND (`what order am I on` EQUALS `an assessment order` OR `what order am I on` EQUALS `a court assessment order` OR `what order am I on` EQUALS `a temporary treatment order` OR `what order am I on` EQUALS `a treatment order`))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `what order am I on` EQUALS `a treatment order` AND `am I also on an intensive monitored supervision order`
         THEN `yes or no` (`is the leave for urgent or necessary medical treatment elsewhere` AND `how many days of leave` AT MOST 7)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 217 "An authorised psychiatrist may revoke a leave of absence ... by written notice and require the person to return
-- ... if the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that -- (a) revocation of the leave of absence is necessary to prevent
-- -- (i) serious deterioration in the person's mental or physical health; or (ii) serious harm to the person or to
-- another person; or (b) the person has failed to comply with a condition to which the leave of absence is subject; or
-- (c) the purpose for the leave of absence no longer exists." An "if": JUST FALSE where none holds.
@export Can my leave of absence be revoked and can I be required to return (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 217)? Only by written notice, if the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that revoking it is necessary to prevent serious deterioration or serious harm, that I broke a condition of the leave, or that its purpose no longer exists.
GIVEN `is revocation necessary to prevent serious deterioration or harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that revoking the leave is necessary to prevent serious deterioration in your mental or physical health, or serious harm to you or another person
      `did I fail to comply with a condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that you failed to comply with a condition of the leave
      `has the purpose of the leave ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that the purpose of the leave no longer exists
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my leave be revoked` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`is revocation necessary to prevent serious deterioration or harm` OR `did I fail to comply with a condition` OR `has the purpose of the leave ended`)

§§ `Second psychiatric opinions` -- arises if you are on a temporary treatment order, treatment order, secure treatment order or forensic order

-- s 67 "(1) An eligible patient may seek a second psychiatric opinion at any time. (2) The following may seek a second
-- psychiatric opinion -- (a) any person, at the request of the eligible patient; (b) a guardian of the eligible patient;
-- (c) a parent of the eligible patient, if the eligible patient is under the age of 16 years; (d) the DFFH Secretary, if
-- that Secretary has parental responsibility". A patient who is not an "eligible patient" (an assessment patient), a
-- mental health advocate and anyone else: NOTHING (NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*). s 68: from any
-- psychiatrist. s 69(2): the second psychiatrist cannot override the treatment prescribed.
@export Can this person seek a second psychiatric opinion about my order and treatment (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 67, 68)? An eligible patient (on a temporary treatment, treatment, secure treatment or forensic order) may seek one at any time from any psychiatrist, and so may a person I ask, my guardian, my parent if I am under 16, or the DFFH Secretary if they have parental responsibility for me.
GIVEN `what order am I on` IS AN `Order` @desc The order you are on
      `who is seeking it` IS A `Who is acting` @desc Who is seeking the second opinion: you, a person you asked, your guardian, your parent, a mental health advocate, the DFFH Secretary (who has parental responsibility for you), or someone else
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I get a second psychiatric opinion` MEANS
    IF     (NOT (`s 3 -- an eligible patient` `what order am I on`))
        OR `who is seeking it` EQUALS `a mental health advocate`
        OR `who is seeking it` EQUALS `someone else`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `yes or no` (NOT (`who is seeking it` EQUALS `my parent` AND `my age` AT LEAST 16))

DECLARE `Reasons owed` IS ONE OF
    `the psychiatrist decided the criteria still apply after a second opinion said they do not`
    `the psychiatrist adopted none or only some of a second opinion's recommended changes`
    `the psychiatrist overrode my advance statement of preferences`
    `none of these`

-- ss 73(2)-(3), 74(3)-(4), 90(2), with the duty from mhw-rules.l4. s 73 applies to a patient other than a forensic
-- patient; the order is not asked, since the decision the person names fixes the section.
@export Did the authorised psychiatrist give me written reasons in time (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 73, 74, 90)? Written reasons are due within 10 business days when, after a second psychiatric opinion, the psychiatrist decides the order's criteria still apply or does not adopt all its recommended changes, or when the psychiatrist overrides my advance statement of preferences.
GIVEN `what did the psychiatrist decide` IS A `Reasons owed` @desc What the authorised psychiatrist decided: that the order's criteria still apply after a second opinion said they do not (s 73), to adopt none or only some of a second opinion's recommended changes (s 74), to make a treatment decision against your advance statement of preferences (s 90), or none of these
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the authorised psychiatrist made the determination or decision
      `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 10 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the period (0 if none)
      `have I been given written reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been given the written reasons
      `the day I was given them` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given the written reasons (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Did I get written reasons in time` MEANS
    IF `what did the psychiatrist decide` EQUALS `none of these`
    THEN `not owed on these facts`
    ELSE `what became of the duty from` `the day of the decision` `to` (`the last of` 10 `business days after` `the day of the decision` `with` `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 10 business days`) `under` `ss 73, 74, 90 -- the authorised psychiatrist must give me written reasons within 10 business days` `owed by` `the authorised psychiatrist` `to do` `give me written reasons` `done` `have I been given written reasons` `on` `the day I was given them` `as at` `today`

DECLARE `Recommendations adopted` IS ONE OF
    `none of them`
    `only some of them`
    `all of them`

-- s 75 "(1) If the authorised psychiatrist decides to adopt none or only some of the recommended changes made in the
-- report under section 72, the eligible patient or a person specified in section 67(2) may apply to the chief
-- psychiatrist to review the treatment of the patient." An "if": JUST FALSE where all were adopted or none were
-- recommended. Anyone not the patient or in s 67(2): NOTHING. s 75(4): treatment may continue during the review.
@export Can this person ask the chief psychiatrist to review my treatment (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 75)? Yes, if a second psychiatric opinion recommended changes to my treatment and the authorised psychiatrist adopted none or only some of them; I may apply, and so may a person I ask, my guardian, my parent if I am under 16, or the DFFH Secretary.
GIVEN `did the second opinion recommend changes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the second psychiatric opinion report recommended changes to your treatment
      `how many were adopted` IS A `Recommendations adopted` @desc How many of the recommended changes the authorised psychiatrist decided to adopt: none of them, only some of them, or all of them
      `who is applying` IS A `Who is acting` @desc Who is applying: you, a person you asked, your guardian, your parent, a mental health advocate, the DFFH Secretary, or someone else
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I ask the chief psychiatrist to review my treatment` MEANS
    IF `who is applying` EQUALS `a mental health advocate` OR `who is applying` EQUALS `someone else`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `yes or no` (    `did the second opinion recommend changes`
                      AND (NOT (`how many were adopted` EQUALS `all of them`))
                      AND (NOT (`who is applying` EQUALS `my parent` AND `my age` AT LEAST 16)))

-- s 76(1), with the duty from mhw-rules.l4.
@export Did the chief psychiatrist review my treatment in time (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 76)? The review is due within 10 business days after the chief psychiatrist receives the application.
GIVEN `the day the chief psychiatrist received the application` IS A DATE @desc The day the chief psychiatrist received the application for review of your treatment
      `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 10 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the period (0 if none)
      `has the review been done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the chief psychiatrist has reviewed your treatment
      `the day of the review` IS A DATE @desc The day the chief psychiatrist completed the review (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Was my treatment reviewed in time` MEANS
    `what became of the duty from` `the day the chief psychiatrist received the application` `to` (`the last of` 10 `business days after` `the day the chief psychiatrist received the application` `with` `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 10 business days`) `under` `s 76(1) -- the chief psychiatrist must review my treatment within 10 business days` `owed by` `the chief psychiatrist` `to do` `review my treatment` `done` `has the review been done` `on` `the day of the review` `as at` `today`

§§ `Consent and treatment`

-- s 87(1), from mhw-rules.l4. s 85(2): "The person seeking the informed consent must presume that the person whose
-- consent is sought has the capacity to give it."
@export Do I have capacity to give informed consent to this treatment (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 87)? I have it if I can understand the information, remember it, use or weigh it, and communicate my decision in any way. Capacity is presumed, is specific to the decision, and is not lost just because a decision seems unwise.
GIVEN `can I understand the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to understand the information you are given to decide whether or not to consent (with appropriate supports)
      `can I remember it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to remember that information
      `can I use or weigh it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to use or weigh that information in deciding
      `can I communicate my decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are able to communicate your decision by speech, gestures or any other means
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I have capacity to give informed consent` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`s 87 -- I have capacity to give informed consent` `can I understand the information` `can I remember it` `can I use or weigh it` `can I communicate my decision`)

-- s 86 "(1) Informed consent may be given by a person if the person -- (a) has capacity ...; and (b) has been given
-- adequate information ...; and (c) has been given a reasonable opportunity to decide ...; and (d) has given consent
-- freely without undue pressure or coercion ...; and (e) has not withdrawn their consent or indicated their intention to
-- withdraw their consent." (2) adequate information is an explanation of (a) the treatment, its purpose, type, method
-- and likely duration, (b) its advantages and disadvantages, discomfort, risks and side effects, (c) beneficial
-- alternatives, (d) answers to questions, (e) the advantages and disadvantages of not having it, (f) other relevant
-- information likely to influence the decision, (g) for treatment, a statement of rights. (3) a reasonable opportunity is
-- (a) a reasonable period of time, (b) a reasonable opportunity to discuss with the practitioner, (c) appropriate
-- supports, (d) a reasonable opportunity to get other advice. Each "if" is read as a full test (fork F5).
@export Have I given informed consent to this treatment (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 86)? Only if I have capacity, was given the information the Act lists and a reasonable opportunity to decide, consented freely without undue pressure or coercion, and have not withdrawn it.
GIVEN `do I have capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have capacity to give informed consent to this decision (s 87: you can understand, remember, use or weigh the information and communicate your decision)
      `was the treatment explained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given an explanation of the proposed treatment, including its purpose, type, method and likely duration
      `were its advantages, disadvantages, risks and side effects explained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given an explanation of its advantages and disadvantages, including discomfort, risks and common or expected side effects
      `were the alternatives explained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given an explanation of any beneficial alternative treatments reasonably available, with their advantages and disadvantages
      `were my questions answered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given answers to any relevant questions you asked
      `was not having it explained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given an explanation of the advantages and disadvantages of not having the treatment
      `was I given other relevant information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given any other relevant information likely to influence your decision
      `was I given a statement of rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, for treatment for mental illness, you were given a statement of rights relevant to your situation (answer yes for medical treatment, where it is not required)
      `did I have reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given a reasonable period of time to consider the decision
      `could I discuss it with the practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a reasonable opportunity to discuss it with the practitioner proposing the treatment
      `was I given appropriate supports` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given appropriate supports to make the decision
      `could I get other advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a reasonable opportunity to get other advice or assistance
      `did I consent freely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave consent freely, without undue pressure or coercion by anyone
      `have I withdrawn or said I will withdraw` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have withdrawn your consent or indicated that you intend to withdraw it
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Have I given informed consent` MEANS
    `yes or no` (    `do I have capacity`
                 AND `adequate information`
                 AND `a reasonable opportunity`
                 AND `did I consent freely`
                 AND (NOT `have I withdrawn or said I will withdraw`))
    WHERE
        `adequate information` MEANS
                `was the treatment explained` AND `were its advantages, disadvantages, risks and side effects explained` AND `were the alternatives explained`
            AND `were my questions answered` AND `was not having it explained` AND `was I given other relevant information` AND `was I given a statement of rights`
        `a reasonable opportunity` MEANS
            `did I have reasonable time` AND `could I discuss it with the practitioner` AND `was I given appropriate supports` AND `could I get other advice`

DECLARE `Kind of treatment` IS ONE OF
    `treatment for mental illness other than electroconvulsive treatment or neurosurgery`
    `electroconvulsive treatment`
    `neurosurgery for mental illness`

DECLARE `Treatment without consent answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the authorised psychiatrist may make the treatment decision for me`
    `no: the authorised psychiatrist is not satisfied it is clinically appropriate and the least restrictive way`
    `no: it departs from the treatment I prefer in my advance statement and neither ground for overriding it is met`
    `no need: I have capacity and I consent`
    `not under s 89: electroconvulsive treatment and neurosurgery need the Tribunal or my own written consent`
    `not under s 89: on an assessment order or court assessment order only ss 160 and 175 apply`
    `s 89 does not reach me: I am not a patient`

-- s 89 "(1) This section applies if -- (a) a patient (other than an assessment patient or a court assessment patient) --
-- (i) does not have capacity to give informed consent to treatment proposed by an authorised psychiatrist; or (ii) has
-- capacity ... but does not give informed consent ...; and (b) the treatment proposed ... is not electroconvulsive
-- treatment or neurosurgery for mental illness ... (3) An authorised psychiatrist may make a treatment decision for a
-- patient under this section if the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that -- (a) the treatment is clinically
-- appropriate; and (b) there is no less restrictive way for the patient to be treated". s 90(1) "An authorised
-- psychiatrist may only make a treatment decision ... that is not in accordance with the preferred treatment specified in
-- the patient's advance statement of preference if the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that the patient's preferred
-- treatment -- (a) is not clinically appropriate; or (b) is clinically appropriate but is unable to be provided ...
-- despite the designated mental health service making all reasonable efforts to do so." s 89(2): only the patient's own
-- consent counts, not a refusal by anyone authorised to decide for them.
@export Can I be given treatment for mental illness without my consent (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 89, 90)? If I am a patient on a temporary treatment, treatment, secure or forensic order and I lack capacity or do not consent, the authorised psychiatrist may decide my treatment if satisfied it is clinically appropriate and there is no less restrictive way; going against my advance statement needs a further reason.
GIVEN `what order am I on` IS AN `Order` @desc The order you are on
      `what treatment is proposed` IS A `Kind of treatment` @desc The kind of treatment proposed: treatment for mental illness other than electroconvulsive treatment or neurosurgery, electroconvulsive treatment, or neurosurgery for mental illness
      `do I have capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have capacity to give informed consent to the proposed treatment (s 87)
      `do I give informed consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you give informed consent to the proposed treatment
      `is the psychiatrist satisfied it is clinically appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that the treatment is clinically appropriate
      `is the psychiatrist satisfied there is no less restrictive way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that there is no less restrictive way for you to be treated (having regard to your views and preferences, your advance statement, your support person and others, s 89(4))
      `does it depart from my advance statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proposed treatment is not the treatment you prefer in an advance statement of preferences that is in effect (answer no if you have none)
      `is my preferred treatment not clinically appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that the treatment you prefer is not clinically appropriate
      `can my preferred treatment not be provided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that the treatment you prefer is clinically appropriate but cannot be provided by the service despite all reasonable efforts
GIVETH A `Treatment without consent answer`
`Can I be treated without my consent` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 3 -- a patient` `what order am I on`)
    THEN `s 89 does not reach me: I am not a patient`
    ELSE IF `what order am I on` EQUALS `an assessment order` OR `what order am I on` EQUALS `a court assessment order`
         THEN `not under s 89: on an assessment order or court assessment order only ss 160 and 175 apply`
         ELSE IF NOT (`what treatment is proposed` EQUALS `treatment for mental illness other than electroconvulsive treatment or neurosurgery`)
              THEN `not under s 89: electroconvulsive treatment and neurosurgery need the Tribunal or my own written consent`
              ELSE IF `do I have capacity` AND `do I give informed consent`
                   THEN `no need: I have capacity and I consent`
                   ELSE IF NOT (`is the psychiatrist satisfied it is clinically appropriate` AND `is the psychiatrist satisfied there is no less restrictive way`)
                        THEN `no: the authorised psychiatrist is not satisfied it is clinically appropriate and the least restrictive way`
                        ELSE IF `does it depart from my advance statement` AND (NOT (`is my preferred treatment not clinically appropriate` OR `can my preferred treatment not be provided`))
                             THEN `no: it departs from the treatment I prefer in my advance statement and neither ground for overriding it is met`
                             ELSE `yes: the authorised psychiatrist may make the treatment decision for me`

DECLARE `Medical treatment decider` IS ONE OF
    `I decide: I have capacity, and it may be given if I give informed consent`
    `my medical treatment decision maker`
    `a person VCAT appointed to decide about this treatment`
    `my guardian under a guardianship order with power over this treatment`
    `a person with legal authority to consent for me`
    `the authorised psychiatrist, if satisfied it would benefit me`
    `no one yet: the authorised psychiatrist must not consent while I am likely to regain capacity soon`

-- s 91 "If a patient gives informed consent to medical treatment, the medical treatment may be given". s 92 "(1) If a
-- patient who is of or over the age of 18 years does not have capacity to give informed consent to medical treatment,
-- the medical treatment may be given ... with the consent of the first of the following persons who is reasonably
-- available, willing and able to make a decision ... (a) the patient's medical treatment decision maker; (b) a person
-- appointed by VCAT ...; (c) a person appointed under a guardianship order ...; (d) subject to section 93, the
-- authorised psychiatrist. (2) If a patient who is under the age of 18 years does not have capacity ... (a) a person who
-- has the legal authority to consent ... and who is reasonably available, willing and able ...; or (b) if a person
-- referred to in paragraph (a) is not reasonably available or is not willing and able ..., subject to section 93, the
-- authorised psychiatrist." s 93 "(1) ... may consent ... if the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that the medical
-- treatment would benefit the patient ... (3) If the authorised psychiatrist is of the opinion that the patient does not
-- currently have capacity ... but is likely to have that capacity within a reasonable period of time, the authorised
-- psychiatrist must not give consent ... (4) Despite subsection (3), the authorised psychiatrist may give consent ... if
-- the delay ... could result in serious harm to, or deterioration in, the mental or physical health of the patient."
-- Medical treatment is treatment for a condition other than mental illness. Not a patient: NOTHING (the Medical Treatment
-- Planning and Decisions Act 2016 governs).
@export Who may consent to medical treatment (not treatment for mental illness) for me while I am a patient (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 91, 92, 93)? If I have capacity, I decide; if not, the first available, willing and able of my medical treatment decision maker, a VCAT appointee and my guardian (for a person under 18, whoever has legal authority), and only then the authorised psychiatrist.
GIVEN `what order am I on` IS AN `Order` @desc The order you are on (this question is for a patient)
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `do I have capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have capacity to give informed consent to the medical treatment (s 87)
      `is my medical treatment decision maker available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an adult: whether your medical treatment decision maker (Medical Treatment Planning and Decisions Act 2016) is reasonably available, willing and able to decide
      `is a VCAT appointee available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an adult: whether a person appointed by VCAT to decide about this treatment is reasonably available, willing and able
      `is my guardian available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an adult: whether a guardian appointed under a guardianship order with power over this treatment is reasonably available, willing and able
      `is a person with legal authority available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a person under 18: whether a person with legal authority to consent for you (for example a parent) is reasonably available, willing and able
      `am I likely to regain capacity soon` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist thinks you are likely to have capacity within a reasonable period of time
      `could delay cause serious harm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether delaying the treatment could result in serious harm to, or deterioration in, your mental or physical health
GIVETH A MAYBE `Medical treatment decider`
`Who may consent to my medical treatment` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 3 -- a patient` `what order am I on`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `do I have capacity`
         THEN JUST `I decide: I have capacity, and it may be given if I give informed consent`
         ELSE IF `my age` AT LEAST 18
              THEN IF `is my medical treatment decision maker available`
                   THEN JUST `my medical treatment decision maker`
                   ELSE IF `is a VCAT appointee available`
                        THEN JUST `a person VCAT appointed to decide about this treatment`
                        ELSE IF `is my guardian available`
                             THEN JUST `my guardian under a guardianship order with power over this treatment`
                             ELSE `the psychiatrist route`
              ELSE IF `is a person with legal authority available`
                   THEN JUST `a person with legal authority to consent for me`
                   ELSE `the psychiatrist route`
    WHERE
        `the psychiatrist route` MEANS
            IF `am I likely to regain capacity soon` AND (NOT `could delay cause serious harm`)
            THEN JUST `no one yet: the authorised psychiatrist must not consent while I am likely to regain capacity soon`
            ELSE JUST `the authorised psychiatrist, if satisfied it would benefit me`

§§ `Electroconvulsive treatment and neurosurgery` -- arises if electroconvulsive treatment or neurosurgery for mental illness is proposed for you

-- s 94 "Electroconvulsive treatment must not be performed on a person other than in accordance with this Part." s 98
-- (adult patient) and s 103 (adult not a patient): "may be performed ... if -- (a) the adult ... has personally given
-- informed consent in writing ...; or (b) the Mental Health Tribunal has made an order authorising a course of
-- electroconvulsive treatment". s 108 (young patient) and s 113 (young person not a patient): only if the Tribunal has
-- made an order. A flat "must not ... other than": JUST FALSE otherwise. The order must be one whose course has not
-- ended (ss 102, 107, 112, 117).
@export Can electroconvulsive treatment (ECT) be performed on me (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 94, 98, 103, 108, 113)? If I am 18 or over, only with my own written informed consent or a Mental Health Tribunal order authorising a course of it; if I am under 18, only with a Tribunal order.
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `have I given written informed consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have personally given informed consent in writing to receiving the electroconvulsive treatment
      `is there a Tribunal order for a course that has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Mental Health Tribunal has made an order authorising a course of electroconvulsive treatment for you, and the course has not ended
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can electroconvulsive treatment be performed on me` MEANS
    IF `my age` AT LEAST 18
    THEN `yes or no` (`have I given written informed consent` OR `is there a Tribunal order for a course that has not ended`)
    ELSE `yes or no` `is there a Tribunal order for a course that has not ended`

DECLARE `ECT order answer` IS ONE OF
    `the Tribunal must make an order authorising a course of electroconvulsive treatment`
    `the Tribunal must make an order refusing the treatment`

-- s 100 (adult patient): authorise if satisfied "(i) the patient does not have capacity to give informed consent ...;
-- and (ii) there is no less restrictive way for the patient to be treated". s 105 (adult not a patient): those two "and
-- (iii) either -- (A) the person has an instructional directive giving informed consent to electroconvulsive treatment;
-- or (B) the person does not have an instructional directive ... and the person's medical treatment decision maker gives
-- informed consent in writing". s 110 (young patient): "(i) the young patient has given their informed consent in
-- writing ...; or (ii) the young patient does not have capacity ... and there is no less restrictive way". s 115 (young
-- person not a patient): "(i) ... has given their informed consent in writing ...; or (ii) ... does not have capacity
-- ...; and (A) the young person's medical treatment decision maker has given informed consent in writing ...; and (B)
-- there is no less restrictive way". Otherwise the Tribunal "must ... make an order refusing".
@export Must the Mental Health Tribunal authorise a course of electroconvulsive treatment for me, or refuse it (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 100, 105, 110, 115)? For an adult it must be satisfied I lack capacity to consent and there is no less restrictive way (and, if I am not a patient, that my instructional directive or my medical treatment decision maker consents); for a person under 18, it may also authorise it on my own written consent.
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `am I a patient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a patient under the Act (on an assessment, court assessment, temporary treatment, treatment, secure treatment or forensic order)
      `have I given written informed consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given informed consent in writing to the course of electroconvulsive treatment
      `is the Tribunal satisfied I lack capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that you do not have capacity to give informed consent to the electroconvulsive treatment
      `is the Tribunal satisfied there is no less restrictive way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that there is no less restrictive way for you to be treated
      `do I have an instructional directive consenting to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an instructional directive (advance care directive) giving informed consent to electroconvulsive treatment
      `has my medical treatment decision maker consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your medical treatment decision maker has given informed consent in writing to the course
GIVETH AN `ECT order answer`
`Must the Tribunal authorise electroconvulsive treatment` MEANS
    IF `authorised` THEN `the Tribunal must make an order authorising a course of electroconvulsive treatment` ELSE `the Tribunal must make an order refusing the treatment`
    WHERE
        `lacks capacity and no less restrictive way` MEANS `is the Tribunal satisfied I lack capacity` AND `is the Tribunal satisfied there is no less restrictive way`
        `authorised` MEANS
            IF `my age` AT LEAST 18
            THEN IF `am I a patient`
                 THEN `lacks capacity and no less restrictive way`
                 ELSE `lacks capacity and no less restrictive way` AND (`do I have an instructional directive consenting to it` OR `has my medical treatment decision maker consented in writing`)
            ELSE IF `am I a patient`
                 THEN `have I given written informed consent` OR `lacks capacity and no less restrictive way`
                 ELSE `have I given written informed consent` OR (`lacks capacity and no less restrictive way` AND `has my medical treatment decision maker consented in writing`)

-- s 95 "a course of electroconvulsive treatment means treatment specified by the Mental Health Tribunal in an order
-- under this Part that is -- (a) up to 12 electroconvulsive treatments; and (b) performed within a period of time that
-- does not exceed 6 months." s 96(1)(a): the order's expiry date "must be no more than 6 months after the date on which
-- the order is made"; (b) "no more than 12 treatments".
@export What is the latest date a Mental Health Tribunal order for a course of electroconvulsive treatment can run to (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 95, 96)? No more than 6 months after the date the order is made, and for no more than 12 treatments.
GIVEN `the day the order was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the Mental Health Tribunal made the order authorising the course
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the latest date my electroconvulsive treatment order can run to` MEANS
    `the date` 6 `months after` `the day the order was made`

-- s 102 (adult patient), s 107 (adult not a patient), s 112 (young patient), s 117 (young person not a patient): "The
-- course of electroconvulsive treatment ends at the earliest of the following": all treatments performed; the
-- completion date reached; the person ceases to be, or (if not a patient) becomes, a patient; capacity regained (for a
-- young person authorised on capacity, the psychiatrist "determines" it); the psychiatrist determines (or, for a young
-- person, is no longer satisfied) that it is no longer the least restrictive treatment; a new order; for s 107 and s 117,
-- the medical treatment decision maker withdraws consent; for ss 112, 117, a young person authorised on their own consent
-- withdraws it, and reaching 18. A closed list of the ways the course ends: JUST FALSE where none has happened. The
-- completion date is read as reached on that day (fork F10).
@export Has my course of electroconvulsive treatment ended (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 102, 107, 112, 117)? It ends when all authorised treatments are given, the order's completion date is reached, my status as a patient changes, I regain capacity, it is no longer the least restrictive treatment, a new order is made, consent it rests on is withdrawn, or (if I am under 18) I turn 18.
GIVEN `was I 18 or over when it was authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were 18 or over when the Tribunal authorised the course
      `was I a patient when it was authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a patient under the Act when the Tribunal authorised the course
      `was it authorised on my own written consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a person under 18: whether the Tribunal authorised it because you gave informed consent in writing (rather than because you lacked capacity)
      `treatments given` IS A NUMBER @desc How many electroconvulsive treatments of the course have been given
      `treatments authorised` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum number of treatments the order authorised (no more than 12)
      `the completion date` IS A DATE @desc The date by which the order says the course must be completed
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `has my patient status changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have stopped being a patient (if you were one) or become a patient (if you were not)
      `have I regained capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have regained capacity to give informed consent to the treatment (for a person under 18 authorised for lack of capacity, whether the psychiatrist has determined so)
      `is it no longer the least restrictive treatment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the psychiatrist has determined (or, for a person under 18, is no longer satisfied) that electroconvulsive treatment is the least restrictive treatment available
      `has a new order been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has made a new electroconvulsive treatment order for you
      `has the consent it rests on been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the consent the order rests on has been withdrawn: your own (if under 18 and authorised on your consent) or your medical treatment decision maker's (if you are not a patient)
      `have I turned 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a person under 18 when it was authorised: whether you have since turned 18
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Has my course of electroconvulsive treatment ended` MEANS
    `yes or no` (   `treatments given` AT LEAST `treatments authorised`
                 OR (NOT (`today` `is before` `the completion date`))
                 OR `has my patient status changed`
                 OR `has a new order been made`
                 OR `the ways that depend on the kind of order`)
    WHERE
        `the ways that depend on the kind of order` MEANS
            IF `was I 18 or over when it was authorised`
            THEN    `have I regained capacity`
                 OR `is it no longer the least restrictive treatment`
                 OR ((NOT `was I a patient when it was authorised`) AND `has the consent it rests on been withdrawn`)
            ELSE    `have I turned 18`
                 OR (IF `was it authorised on my own written consent`
                     THEN `has the consent it rests on been withdrawn`
                     ELSE    `have I regained capacity`
                          OR `is it no longer the least restrictive treatment`
                          OR ((NOT `was I a patient when it was authorised`) AND `has the consent it rests on been withdrawn`))

-- s 97(1), with the duty from mhw-rules.l4; s 97(2), (3): on an urgent request, "as soon as practicable" (no fixed day;
-- not encoded as a deadline).
@export Was the Mental Health Tribunal's hearing of the application for electroconvulsive treatment on me listed and completed in time (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 97)? Within 5 business days after the Tribunal receives the application (sooner, as soon as practicable, if urgent).
GIVEN `the day the Tribunal received the application` IS A DATE @desc The day the Mental Health Tribunal received the application
      `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 5 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the period (0 if none)
      `has the hearing been completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has listed and completed the hearing
      `the day it was completed` IS A DATE @desc The day the hearing was completed (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Was my electroconvulsive treatment hearing in time` MEANS
    `what became of the duty from` `the day the Tribunal received the application` `to` (`the last of` 5 `business days after` `the day the Tribunal received the application` `with` `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 5 business days`) `under` `s 97(1) -- the Tribunal must hear the electroconvulsive treatment application within 5 business days` `owed by` `the Mental Health Tribunal` `to do` `hold the hearing` `done` `has the hearing been completed` `on` `the day it was completed` `as at` `today`

-- s 119 "Neurosurgery for mental illness must not be performed on a person unless the Mental Health Tribunal has
-- approved the neurosurgery by order under section 121." s 121(2) "The Mental Health Tribunal must not approve
-- neurosurgery ... unless it is satisfied that -- (a) the person ... has given informed consent in writing to the
-- neurosurgery; and (b) the neurosurgery for mental illness will benefit the person." Both "must not ... unless": JUST
-- FALSE where they fail. Read together: the Tribunal's order is lawful only on those two (fork F11 treats an approval
-- without them as no approval).
@export Can neurosurgery for mental illness be performed on me (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 119, 120, 121)? Only if the Mental Health Tribunal has approved it by order, and it may approve only if I have given informed consent in writing and it is satisfied the neurosurgery will benefit me.
GIVEN `have I given written informed consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have personally given informed consent in writing to the neurosurgery
      `is the Tribunal satisfied it will benefit me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Mental Health Tribunal is satisfied that the neurosurgery will benefit you (considering whether it is likely to remedy or alleviate the illness, the consequences of not having it, alternatives, and its risks and side effects)
      `has the Tribunal approved it by order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has made an order approving the neurosurgery
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can neurosurgery be performed on me` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`has the Tribunal approved it by order` AND `have I given written informed consent` AND `is the Tribunal satisfied it will benefit me`)

-- s 124, with the duty from mhw-rules.l4.
@export Did the Mental Health Tribunal hear and decide the application for neurosurgery for mental illness in time (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 124)? Within 30 business days after it receives the application.
GIVEN `the day the Tribunal received the application` IS A DATE @desc The day the Mental Health Tribunal received the application
      `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 30 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the period (0 if none)
      `has the Tribunal decided it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has heard and determined the application
      `the day it was decided` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tribunal determined it (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Was my neurosurgery application decided in time` MEANS
    `what became of the duty from` `the day the Tribunal received the application` `to` (`the last of` 30 `business days after` `the day the Tribunal received the application` `with` `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 30 business days`) `under` `s 124 -- the Tribunal must determine the neurosurgery application within 30 business days` `owed by` `the Mental Health Tribunal` `to do` `hold the hearing` `done` `has the Tribunal decided it` `on` `the day it was decided` `as at` `today`

§§ `Seclusion and restraint` -- arises if you are receiving services in a designated mental health service

DECLARE `Restrictive intervention` IS ONE OF
    `seclusion`
    `physical restraint`
    `mechanical restraint`
    `chemical restraint`

DECLARE `Purpose of the intervention` IS ONE OF
    `to prevent imminent and serious harm to me or another person`
    `to give me treatment or medical treatment`
    `another purpose`

DECLARE `Who authorised it` IS ONE OF
    `an authorised psychiatrist`
    `a registered medical practitioner`
    `a nurse in charge`
    `a nurse practitioner acting within their ordinary scope of practice`
    `a registered nurse`
    `no one`

-- s 127 "A restrictive intervention may be used ... for the following purposes only -- (a) to prevent imminent and
-- serious harm to that person or another person; (b) in the case of bodily restraint -- to administer treatment or
-- medical treatment to the person." s 128 "(1) ... may only be used ... if it is necessary to achieve a purpose specified
-- in section 127. (2) A restrictive intervention must not be used ... unless all reasonable and less restrictive options
-- have been tried or considered and have been found to be unsuitable." s 132 "(1) The use of seclusion or bodily
-- restraint ... must be authorised by -- (a) an authorised psychiatrist; or (b) if an authorised psychiatrist is not
-- reasonably available, a registered medical practitioner or a nurse in charge. (2) The use of chemical restraint ... must
-- be authorised by -- (a) an authorised psychiatrist; or (b) if an authorised psychiatrist is not reasonably available, a
-- registered medical practitioner or a nurse practitioner acting within their ordinary scope of practice. (3) ... only if
-- satisfied that it is necessary ... (4) ... a registered nurse may authorise the use of physical restraint ... only if
-- -- (a) an authorised psychiatrist, registered medical practitioner or nurse in charge is not immediately available ...;
-- and (b) the registered nurse is satisfied that the use of physical restraint is necessary to achieve a purpose
-- specified in section 127(a)." "Bodily restraint" is physical or mechanical restraint (s 3(1)). Every limb is "only" or
-- "must not ... unless": JUST FALSE where one fails.
@export Can seclusion or restraint be used on me in a designated mental health service (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 126, 127, 128, 132)? Only to prevent imminent and serious harm (or, for physical or mechanical restraint, to give treatment), only if necessary after all reasonable less restrictive options were tried or considered and found unsuitable, and only if authorised by the right person.
GIVEN `what intervention` IS A `Restrictive intervention` @desc The restrictive intervention: seclusion (being confined alone in a room you cannot leave), physical restraint (someone using their body to stop your movement), mechanical restraint (a device), or chemical restraint (a drug given mainly to control behaviour by restricting movement, not as treatment)
      `for what purpose` IS A `Purpose of the intervention` @desc Its purpose: to prevent imminent and serious harm to you or another person, to give you treatment or medical treatment, or another purpose
      `is the authoriser satisfied it is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person authorising it is satisfied it is necessary to achieve that purpose
      `were less restrictive options tried or considered and found unsuitable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all reasonable and less restrictive options were tried or considered and found to be unsuitable
      `who authorised it` IS A `Who authorised it` @desc Who authorised it: an authorised psychiatrist, a registered medical practitioner, a nurse in charge, a nurse practitioner acting within their ordinary scope of practice, a registered nurse, or no one
      `was an authorised psychiatrist reasonably available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an authorised psychiatrist was reasonably available to authorise it
      `was a psychiatrist, doctor or nurse in charge immediately available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For physical restraint authorised by a registered nurse: whether an authorised psychiatrist, registered medical practitioner or nurse in charge was immediately available
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can seclusion or restraint be used on me` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`a permitted purpose` AND `is the authoriser satisfied it is necessary` AND `were less restrictive options tried or considered and found unsuitable` AND `properly authorised`)
    WHERE
        `bodily restraint` MEANS `what intervention` EQUALS `physical restraint` OR `what intervention` EQUALS `mechanical restraint`
        `a permitted purpose` MEANS
               `for what purpose` EQUALS `to prevent imminent and serious harm to me or another person`
            OR (`for what purpose` EQUALS `to give me treatment or medical treatment` AND `bodily restraint`)
        `a doctor or nurse in charge, the psychiatrist being unavailable` MEANS
                (NOT `was an authorised psychiatrist reasonably available`)
            AND (`who authorised it` EQUALS `a registered medical practitioner` OR `who authorised it` EQUALS `a nurse in charge`)
        `a doctor or nurse practitioner, the psychiatrist being unavailable` MEANS
                (NOT `was an authorised psychiatrist reasonably available`)
            AND (`who authorised it` EQUALS `a registered medical practitioner` OR `who authorised it` EQUALS `a nurse practitioner acting within their ordinary scope of practice`)
        `a registered nurse under s 132(4)` MEANS
                `what intervention` EQUALS `physical restraint`
            AND `who authorised it` EQUALS `a registered nurse`
            AND (NOT `was a psychiatrist, doctor or nurse in charge immediately available`)
            AND `for what purpose` EQUALS `to prevent imminent and serious harm to me or another person`
        `properly authorised` MEANS
            IF `what intervention` EQUALS `chemical restraint`
            THEN `who authorised it` EQUALS `an authorised psychiatrist` OR `a doctor or nurse practitioner, the psychiatrist being unavailable`
            ELSE `who authorised it` EQUALS `an authorised psychiatrist` OR `a doctor or nurse in charge, the psychiatrist being unavailable` OR `a registered nurse under s 132(4)`

-- s 137 "(2) ... (a) in the case of a person who is subject to bodily restraint, ensure that the person is continuously
-- observed by a registered nurse or a registered medical practitioner for the entire period of the restraint; and (b) in
-- the case of a person who is subject to chemical restraint, ensure that the person is continuously observed ... for not
-- less than one hour after the chemical restraint is administered. (3) A registered nurse or registered medical
-- practitioner must clinically review a person subject to a restrictive intervention as often as is appropriate ...,
-- but not less frequently than every 15 minutes. (4) Subject to subsection (5), an authorised psychiatrist must examine a
-- person subject to a restrictive intervention as often as the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied is appropriate ...,
-- but not less frequently than every 4 hours. (5) If it is not practicable for an authorised psychiatrist to conduct an
-- examination ..., the person must be examined by a registered medical practitioner when so directed". The minimum
-- frequencies are checked; "as often as is appropriate" is a judgment not asked. JUST FALSE where a "must" was not kept.
@export Was I monitored as the Act requires while I was secluded or restrained (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 137)? Under physical or mechanical restraint I must be watched continuously by a nurse or doctor; after chemical restraint, continuously for at least an hour; a nurse or doctor must review me at least every 15 minutes; and an authorised psychiatrist (or a doctor they direct) must examine me at least every 4 hours.
GIVEN `what intervention` IS A `Restrictive intervention` @desc The restrictive intervention: seclusion, physical restraint, mechanical restraint or chemical restraint
      `was I watched continuously throughout` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For physical or mechanical restraint: whether a registered nurse or doctor continuously observed you for the whole period of the restraint
      `hours I was watched continuously after a chemical restraint` IS A NUMBER @desc For chemical restraint: for how many hours after the drug was given a registered nurse or doctor continuously observed you
      `longest gap between clinical reviews in minutes` IS A NUMBER @desc The longest time, in minutes, between clinical reviews of you by a registered nurse or doctor during the intervention
      `longest gap between psychiatrist examinations in hours` IS A NUMBER @desc The longest time, in hours, between examinations of you by an authorised psychiatrist (or a doctor the psychiatrist directed) during the intervention
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I monitored as required` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`observation kept` AND `longest gap between clinical reviews in minutes` AT MOST 15 AND `longest gap between psychiatrist examinations in hours` AT MOST 4)
    WHERE
        `observation kept` MEANS
            CONSIDER `what intervention`
            WHEN `physical restraint` THEN `was I watched continuously throughout`
            WHEN `mechanical restraint` THEN `was I watched continuously throughout`
            WHEN `chemical restraint` THEN `hours I was watched continuously after a chemical restraint` AT LEAST 1
            WHEN `seclusion` THEN TRUE

§§ `My rights as an inpatient, my advance statement and my nominated support person`

DECLARE `Contact` IS ONE OF
    `my legal representative`
    `the chief psychiatrist`
    `the Mental Health and Wellbeing Commission`
    `the Mental Health Tribunal`
    `a community visitor`
    `a mental health advocate or non-legal advocacy service`
    `the DFFH Secretary, who has parental responsibility for me`
    `a prescribed person or body`
    `anyone else`

-- s 53(1) "Subject to this Part, an inpatient has a right to communicate lawfully with any person". s 54 "(1) Subject to
-- subsection (2), an authorised psychiatrist in writing may direct staff ... to restrict an inpatient's right to
-- communicate. (2) A direction under subsection (1) may be made only if the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied that the
-- restriction is reasonably necessary to protect the health, safety and wellbeing of the inpatient or of another person.
-- (3) A direction cannot be made under subsection (1) which restricts an inpatient's right to communicate with -- (a) a
-- legal representative; or (b) the chief psychiatrist; or (c) the Mental Health and Wellbeing Commission; or (d) the
-- Mental Health Tribunal; or (e) a community visitor; or (f) a non-legal mental health advocacy service provider or a
-- mental health advocate; or (g) the DFFH Secretary, if that Secretary has parental responsibility ...; or (h) a
-- prescribed person or body." "only if", "cannot" and "in writing": JUST FALSE where they fail. A person who is not an
-- inpatient is outside s 54: NOTHING.
@export Can my right to communicate with this person (by letter, phone, electronically or by visits) be restricted while I am an inpatient (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 53, 54)? Only by a written direction of the authorised psychiatrist, only if satisfied it is reasonably necessary to protect my or another person's health, safety and wellbeing, and never for my lawyer, the chief psychiatrist, the Commission, the Tribunal, a community visitor or a mental health advocate.
GIVEN `am I an inpatient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a patient detained in a designated mental health service
      `who is it` IS A `Contact` @desc Who you want to communicate with: your legal representative, the chief psychiatrist, the Mental Health and Wellbeing Commission, the Mental Health Tribunal, a community visitor, a mental health advocate or non-legal advocacy service, the DFFH Secretary (with parental responsibility for you), a prescribed person or body, or anyone else
      `is the psychiatrist satisfied it is reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist is satisfied the restriction is reasonably necessary to protect your health, safety and wellbeing or another person's
      `is the direction in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authorised psychiatrist's direction to restrict is in writing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my communication with this person be restricted` MEANS
    IF NOT `am I an inpatient`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `yes or no` (`who is it` EQUALS `anyone else` AND `is the psychiatrist satisfied it is reasonably necessary` AND `is the direction in writing`)

-- s 58 "(2) An advance statement of preferences must -- (a) be signed and dated by the person making it; and (b) specify
-- any or all of the following ... (i) their preferences relating to treatment; (ii) ... care and support ...; (iii) ...
-- whom may be provided with their health information; (iv) the name and contact details of their nominated support
-- person or advocate; (v) ... any person or organisation to be informed that the person is a patient; and (c) be
-- witnessed by an adult; and (d) include a statement signed by the witness [that the maker understands it, acts freely,
-- was seen to sign, and the witness is an adult] ... (3) An advance statement of preferences is in effect from the time
-- it is made until it is revoked." s 59(1) "An advance statement of preferences is revoked if the person who made it --
-- (a) makes a new advance statement of preferences; or (b) revokes the advance statement of preferences." A statement
-- that does not meet s 58(2) is read as not made (fork F8). "(e) include any other prescribed information": the
-- regulations are not deposited and nothing prescribed is asked.
@export Is my advance statement of preferences in effect (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 57, 58, 59)? It is in effect from when it is made until revoked, if I signed and dated it, it sets out my preferences, and an adult witnessed it and signed the witness statement; making a new one revokes it.
GIVEN `did I sign and date it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you signed and dated the statement
      `does it set out my preferences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it sets out any of: your treatment preferences, your care and support preferences (including supports to help you communicate and decide), who may be given your health information, your nominated support person or advocate, or who should be told you are a patient
      `did an adult witness it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an adult witnessed it
      `did the witness sign the witness statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it includes a statement signed by the witness that, in their opinion, you understood it, made it freely, were seen to sign it, and that the witness is an adult
      `have I revoked it or made a new one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since revoked it (by a signed, dated and witnessed revocation) or made a new advance statement of preferences
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my advance statement in effect` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`did I sign and date it` AND `does it set out my preferences` AND `did an adult witness it` AND `did the witness sign the witness statement` AND (NOT `have I revoked it or made a new one`))

-- s 62 "(2) The nomination of a nominated support person must -- (a) be in writing; and (b) be signed and dated by the
-- person making the nomination; and (c) specify the name and contact details of the person nominated; and (d) be
-- witnessed by an adult; and (e) include a statement by the witness that [the maker understands and may revoke it, acts
-- freely, was seen to sign, and the witness is an adult]. (3) The person nominated ... must not be the person who
-- witnesses the nomination." s 63 "(1) A nomination is made when the nominated support person signs an acceptance form
-- ... (3) A nomination under this Part is in effect from the time it is made until the time it is revoked." s 64 "A
-- nomination is revoked if -- (a) the person who made the nomination -- (i) makes a new nomination; or (ii) revokes the
-- nomination; or (b) the nominated support person resigns". Fork F8 as for the advance statement.
@export Is my nomination of a nominated support person in effect (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 62, 63, 64)? It takes effect when the person I nominate signs an acceptance form, if my nomination is in writing, signed and dated, names them with contact details, and is witnessed by an adult other than them; it ends if I revoke it, make a new one, or they resign.
GIVEN `is it in writing, signed and dated by me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the nomination is in writing and signed and dated by you
      `does it give their name and contact details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it gives the name and contact details of the person you nominate
      `did an adult witness it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an adult witnessed it
      `is the witness the person I nominated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the witness is the person you nominated (they must not be)
      `did the witness make the witness statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it includes the witness's statement that, in their opinion, you understood the nomination and that you may revoke it, made it freely, were seen to sign it, and that the witness is an adult
      `have they signed an acceptance form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you nominated has signed an acceptance form agreeing to be your nominated support person
      `have I revoked it or made a new one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have revoked the nomination or made a new nomination
      `have they resigned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the nominated support person has resigned
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my nominated support person nomination in effect` MEANS
    `yes or no` (    `is it in writing, signed and dated by me` AND `does it give their name and contact details` AND `did an adult witness it`
                 AND (NOT `is the witness the person I nominated`) AND `did the witness make the witness statement` AND `have they signed an acceptance form`
                 AND (NOT `have I revoked it or made a new one`) AND (NOT `have they resigned`))

§§ `Mental Health Tribunal hearings` -- arises if you are the subject of a proceeding before the Mental Health Tribunal

-- s 373(1) "Subject to subsection (3), the following must give a person who is the subject of a proceeding access to any
-- documents in its possession in connection with the proceeding at least 2 business days before the hearing -- (a) a
-- psychiatrist who has applied ... for ... electroconvulsive treatment; (b) if the person is a patient, the authorised
-- psychiatrist ...". (2), (3), (8): the Tribunal may deny access if disclosure may cause serious harm. The latest day
-- leaves 2 business days, the hearing day counted (fork F4).
@export By when must I be given access to the documents for my Mental Health Tribunal hearing (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 373)? At least 2 business days before the hearing, unless the Tribunal has allowed them to be withheld because disclosure may cause serious harm.
GIVEN `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE @desc The day of the Mental Health Tribunal hearing
      `how many weekday public holidays fall just before it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the 2 business days before the hearing (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I get the documents for my hearing` MEANS
    `the latest day` 2 `business days before` `the day of the hearing` `with` `how many weekday public holidays fall just before it`

@export Was I given access to the documents for my Mental Health Tribunal hearing in time (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 373)? The authorised psychiatrist (or the psychiatrist applying for electroconvulsive treatment) must give me access at least 2 business days before the hearing, unless the Tribunal has granted an application to withhold them.
GIVEN `the day of the hearing` IS A DATE @desc The day of the Mental Health Tribunal hearing
      `how many weekday public holidays fall just before it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the 2 business days before the hearing (0 if none)
      `did the Tribunal allow the documents to be withheld` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal granted an application to deny you access because disclosure may cause serious harm to you or another person
      `have I been given access` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been given access to the documents
      `the day I was given access` IS A DATE @desc The day you were given access (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Did I get the documents for my hearing in time` MEANS
    IF `did the Tribunal allow the documents to be withheld`
    THEN `not owed on these facts`
    ELSE IF `have I been given access`
         THEN IF `the day I was given access` `is after` `the deadline`
              THEN `not done in time`
              ELSE `done in time`
         ELSE IF `today` `is after` `the deadline`
              THEN `not done in time`
              ELSE `still open`
    WHERE
        `the deadline` MEANS `the latest day` 2 `business days before` `the day of the hearing` `with` `how many weekday public holidays fall just before it`

-- s 374 "(1) If a person who is the subject of a proceeding in the general division or the special division is subject to
-- a temporary treatment order or a treatment order, the Mental Health Tribunal must not adjourn the hearing to a date
-- that is after the order expires unless the Tribunal is satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist. (2) If a hearing
-- is adjourned under subsection (1), the Mental Health Tribunal may extend the duration of the temporary treatment order
-- or treatment order ... for a period not exceeding 10 business days. (3) The Mental Health Tribunal must not extend the
-- duration ... more than once." All three are "must not ... unless", "not exceeding" or "must not": JUST FALSE.
@export Can the Mental Health Tribunal adjourn my hearing past the end of my temporary treatment order or treatment order and extend the order to cover it (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 374)? Only if it is satisfied exceptional circumstances exist, by no more than 10 business days, and only once.
GIVEN `is the Tribunal satisfied there are exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist
      `has the order already been extended under s 374` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has already extended this order once to adjourn a hearing
      `how many business days of extension` IS A NUMBER @desc How many business days the extension would be
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my hearing be adjourned and my order extended` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`is the Tribunal satisfied there are exceptional circumstances` AND (NOT `has the order already been extended under s 374`) AND `how many business days of extension` AT MOST 10)

-- s 376 "The name and other identifying details of a person who is the subject of a proceeding before the Mental Health
-- Tribunal must not be published unless written consent has been obtained from -- (a) the President; and (b) the person
-- who is the subject of a proceeding." "must not ... unless": JUST FALSE without both.
@export Can my name or other identifying details from my Mental Health Tribunal proceeding be published (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 376)? Only with the written consent of both the Tribunal's President and me.
GIVEN `has the President consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the President of the Mental Health Tribunal has given written consent
      `have I consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given written consent
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my name be published` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`has the President consented in writing` AND `have I consented in writing`)

DECLARE `Request timing` IS ONE OF
    `in time`
    `late, but accepted`
    `late: it may be refused`

-- s 380 "(1) After the Mental Health Tribunal has made a determination, a party to a proceeding ... may request a
-- statement of reasons ... (2) The request must -- (a) be in writing; and (b) subject to subsection (3), be received by
-- the Mental Health Tribunal within 20 business days after the Tribunal has made the relevant determination. (3) The
-- Mental Health Tribunal, in its discretion, may accept a request ... received more than 20 business days after".
GIVEN `the day of the determination` IS A DATE
      `weekday public holidays` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 380(2) -- the last day for a request for reasons` `the day of the determination` `weekday public holidays` MEANS
    `the last of` 20 `business days after` `the day of the determination` `with` `weekday public holidays`

@export By when must the Mental Health Tribunal receive my written request for a statement of reasons (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 380)? Within 20 business days after its determination; it may accept a later request in its discretion.
GIVEN `the day of the determination` IS A DATE @desc The day the Mental Health Tribunal made its determination
      `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the period (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I ask for reasons` MEANS
    `s 380(2) -- the last day for a request for reasons` `the day of the determination` `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days`

@export Was my written request to the Mental Health Tribunal for a statement of reasons in time (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 380)? It must be received within 20 business days after the determination, unless the Tribunal accepts a later one in its discretion.
GIVEN `the day of the determination` IS A DATE @desc The day the Mental Health Tribunal made its determination
      `the day the Tribunal received my request` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tribunal received your written request
      `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the period (0 if none)
      `did the Tribunal accept a late request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal, in its discretion, accepted your request although it was late
GIVETH A `Request timing`
`Was my request for reasons in time` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the day the Tribunal received my request` `is after` (`s 380(2) -- the last day for a request for reasons` `the day of the determination` `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days`))
    THEN `in time`
    ELSE IF `did the Tribunal accept a late request`
         THEN `late, but accepted`
         ELSE `late: it may be refused`

-- s 380(4), with the duty from mhw-rules.l4.
@export Did the Mental Health Tribunal give me its statement of reasons in time (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 380(4))? Within 20 business days after it received the request.
GIVEN `the day the Tribunal received my request` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tribunal received your written request for a statement of reasons
      `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the period (0 if none)
      `have I been given the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has given the statement of reasons
      `the day it was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the statement was given (any date if not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`Did I get the statement of reasons in time` MEANS
    `what became of the duty from` `the day the Tribunal received my request` `to` (`the last of` 20 `business days after` `the day the Tribunal received my request` `with` `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days`) `under` `s 380(4) -- the Tribunal must give a statement of reasons within 20 business days` `owed by` `the Mental Health Tribunal` `to do` `give a statement of reasons` `done` `have I been given the statement` `on` `the day it was given` `as at` `today`

-- s 383 "(2) ... an application for review under subsection (1) must be made to VCAT within 20 business days after the
-- later of -- (a) the Mental Health Tribunal's determination; or (b) if the person referred to in subsection (1)
-- requested a statement of reasons, the person's receipt of the statement of reasons. (3) VCAT may accept an application
-- ... after the time specified in subsection (2) if VCAT determines that special circumstances exist."
GIVEN `the day of the determination` IS A DATE
      `I asked for reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I received the reasons` IS A DATE
      `weekday public holidays` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 383(2) -- the last day to apply to VCAT` `the day of the determination` `I asked for reasons` `the day I received the reasons` `weekday public holidays` MEANS
    `the last of` 20 `business days after` `the later day` `with` `weekday public holidays`
    WHERE
        `the later day` MEANS
            IF `I asked for reasons` AND `the day I received the reasons` `is after` `the day of the determination`
            THEN `the day I received the reasons`
            ELSE `the day of the determination`

@export By when must I apply to VCAT for review of a Mental Health Tribunal determination (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 383)? Within 20 business days after the determination or, if I asked for a statement of reasons, after I received it, whichever is later.
GIVEN `the day of the determination` IS A DATE @desc The day the Mental Health Tribunal made its determination
      `did I ask for a statement of reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you requested a statement of reasons under s 380
      `the day I received the statement of reasons` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the statement of reasons (any date if you did not ask)
      `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the period (0 if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply to VCAT` MEANS
    `s 383(2) -- the last day to apply to VCAT` `the day of the determination` `did I ask for a statement of reasons` `the day I received the statement of reasons` `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days`

DECLARE `VCAT review answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, in time`
    `late, but VCAT has found special circumstances and may accept it`
    `no: the 20 business days have passed`
    `no: this determination cannot be reviewed by VCAT`

-- s 383(1) "Subject to subsection (1A), a person who was a party to a proceeding before the Mental Health Tribunal may
-- apply to VCAT for review of any determination made by the Tribunal ... (1A) A determination by the Mental Health
-- Tribunal to refuse an appeal of a decision made in respect of special leave of absence under section 50 of the Crimes
-- (Mental Impairment and Unfitness to be Tried) Act 1997 may not be reviewed by VCAT." s 363(a): the person who is the
-- subject of a proceeding is a party. Not a party: NOTHING (NOTHING-kind *limited by its own wording*).
@export Can I apply to VCAT for review of the Mental Health Tribunal's determination (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 383)? A party (including the person the proceeding is about) may, within 20 business days after the determination or receipt of the reasons; later only if VCAT finds special circumstances.
GIVEN `was I a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a party to the Tribunal proceeding (the person the proceeding is about is always a party)
      `was it a refusal of a special leave appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the determination refused an appeal about special leave of absence under s 50 of the Crimes (Mental Impairment and Unfitness to be Tried) Act 1997
      `the day of the determination` IS A DATE @desc The day the Mental Health Tribunal made its determination
      `did I ask for a statement of reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you requested a statement of reasons
      `the day I received the statement of reasons` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the statement of reasons (any date if you did not ask)
      `the day I apply to VCAT` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply (or would apply) to VCAT
      `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Victorian public holidays fall on a weekday in the period (0 if none)
      `has VCAT found special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether VCAT has determined that special circumstances exist to accept a late application
GIVETH A MAYBE `VCAT review answer`
`Can I apply to VCAT for review` MEANS
    IF NOT `was I a party`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `was it a refusal of a special leave appeal`
         THEN JUST `no: this determination cannot be reviewed by VCAT`
         ELSE IF NOT (`the day I apply to VCAT` `is after` (`s 383(2) -- the last day to apply to VCAT` `the day of the determination` `did I ask for a statement of reasons` `the day I received the statement of reasons` `how many weekday public holidays fall in the 20 business days`))
              THEN JUST `yes, in time`
              ELSE IF `has VCAT found special circumstances`
                   THEN JUST `late, but VCAT has found special circumstances and may accept it`
                   ELSE JUST `no: the 20 business days have passed`

§§ `Complaints to the Mental Health and Wellbeing Commission`

DECLARE `Complainant` IS ONE OF
    `the consumer`
    `another person`
    `a carer, family member or supporter, about their own experience`

DECLARE `Complaint matter` IS ONE OF
    `the service provided to the consumer`
    `a failure to provide a service to the consumer`
    `a failure to make all reasonable efforts to comply with the principles or duties under the Act`
    `how the provider handled a complaint made to it`
    `something else`

DECLARE `Complaint answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, you may complain to the Commission`
    `out of time, but the Commission is satisfied the circumstances require it and may deal with it`
    `no: it is more than 12 months after`

-- s 434 "(1) A person is not entitled to make a complaint to the Mental Health and Wellbeing Commission -- (a) more than
-- 12 months after the matter occurred which is the subject of the complaint; or (b) if the mental health and wellbeing
-- service was not provided, more than 12 months after the mental health and wellbeing service was sought." The last day
-- is the day 12 months after (fork F3).
GIVEN `the service was not provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the matter occurred` IS A DATE
      `the day the service was sought` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 434(1) -- the last day to complain` `the service was not provided` `the day the matter occurred` `the day the service was sought` MEANS
    IF `the service was not provided`
    THEN `the date` 12 `months after` `the day the service was sought`
    ELSE `the date` 12 `months after` `the day the matter occurred`

@export By when must I complain to the Mental Health and Wellbeing Commission (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) s 434)? Within 12 months after the matter happened, or, if the service was never provided, after I sought it; the Commission may deal with a later complaint if satisfied the circumstances require it.
GIVEN `was the service not provided at all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint is that a mental health and wellbeing service you sought was not provided
      `the day the matter occurred` IS A DATE @desc The day the matter you are complaining about occurred
      `the day I sought the service` IS A DATE @desc The day you sought the service (any date if the service was provided)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I complain to the Commission` MEANS
    `s 434(1) -- the last day to complain` `was the service not provided at all` `the day the matter occurred` `the day I sought the service`

-- s 431 (a consumer, about "any matter arising out of -- (a) the provision of a mental health and wellbeing service to
-- the consumer ...; or (b) a failure to provide a mental health and wellbeing service ...; or (c) a failure by a mental
-- health and wellbeing service provider to make all reasonable efforts to comply with the mental health and wellbeing
-- principles or any other principles or duties under this Act; or (d) the manner in which a complaint ... was handled"),
-- s 432 (any other person, the same heads about a consumer), s 433 (a carer, family member or supporter, "in relation to
-- their experience as a carer, family member or supporter of the consumer including" two heads: any matter about their
-- experience); s 434 the 12 months. A matter outside the heads of ss 431, 432: NOTHING (NOTHING-kind *limited by its own
-- wording*). s 438: a complaint made by another person may need the consumer's consent (not encoded).
@export Can I complain to the Mental Health and Wellbeing Commission (Mental Health and Wellbeing Act 2022 (Vic) ss 431-434)? A consumer, or another person, may complain about a mental health and wellbeing service given or not given, a provider's failure to try to comply with the Act's principles or duties, or how a complaint to the provider was handled; a carer, family member or supporter about their own experience; within 12 months, unless the Commission is satisfied the circumstances require it to deal with a later one.
GIVEN `who is complaining` IS A `Complainant` @desc Who is complaining: the consumer (the person who sought or received the service), another person, or a carer, family member or supporter about their own experience
      `what is it about` IS A `Complaint matter` @desc What the complaint is about: the service provided, a failure to provide a service, a failure to make all reasonable efforts to comply with the Act's principles or duties, how the provider handled a complaint, or something else
      `was the service not provided at all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the complaint is that a service sought was not provided
      `the day the matter occurred` IS A DATE @desc The day the matter complained about occurred
      `the day the service was sought` IS A DATE @desc The day the service was sought (any date if it was provided)
      `the day of the complaint` IS A DATE @desc The day you complain (or would complain) to the Commission
      `is the Commission satisfied the circumstances require it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a late complaint: whether the Commission is satisfied that the circumstances of the complaint require it to deal with it
GIVETH A MAYBE `Complaint answer`
`Can I complain to the Commission` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`who is complaining` EQUALS `a carer, family member or supporter, about their own experience`)) AND `what is it about` EQUALS `something else`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF NOT (`the day of the complaint` `is after` (`s 434(1) -- the last day to complain` `was the service not provided at all` `the day the matter occurred` `the day the service was sought`))
         THEN JUST `yes, you may complain to the Commission`
         ELSE IF `is the Commission satisfied the circumstances require it`
              THEN JUST `out of time, but the Commission is satisfied the circumstances require it and may deal with it`
              ELSE JUST `no: it is more than 12 months after`
